---
layout: default
---
{% comment %}
Campaign hub — the "mini home page" for one campaign. Carries the hero, the
at-a-glance stats and the full brief, then hands off to a sub-page per PESO
pillar. The pillar cards deliberately show real substance (the actual op-ed
headline, the actual blog title, what's in the SWOT) rather than bare labels,
so someone who only reads this page still understands the whole campaign.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
Same full-bleed yellow banner every other page on the site opens with. It sits
outside .case-study because that article is width-capped — inside it the band
would stop at 1040px instead of spanning the viewport. It also carries the
page's <h1>, so the hero below doesn't repeat the title.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="call-out call-out_solid">
    <h1 class="call-out_title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
</div>

<article class="case-study"{% if page.accent %} style="--campaign-accent: {{ page.accent }};"{% endif %}>

  <header class="case-hero">
    <div class="case-hero__inner">
      {% if page.concept %}<p class="case-hero__badge">Concept Campaign</p>{% endif %}
      {% if page.tagline %}<p class="case-hero__tagline">&ldquo;{{ page.tagline }}&rdquo;</p>{% endif %}
      <div class="case-hero__meta">
        {% if page.client %}<span><strong>Client</strong> {{ page.client }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if page.industry %}<span><strong>Industry</strong> {{ page.industry | join: ' &middot; ' }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if page.role %}<span><strong>Role</strong> {{ page.role }}</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {% if page.summary %}<p class="case-hero__summary">{{ page.summary }}</p>{% endif %}

      {% if page.at_a_glance %}
      <div class="case-hero__stats">
        {% for item in page.at_a_glance %}
        <div class="case-hero__stat">
          <span class="case-hero__stat-num">{{ item.stat }}</span>
          <span class="case-hero__stat-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if page.concept_note %}<p class="case-hero__note">{{ page.concept_note }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>

  {% if page.overview %}
  <section id="brief" class="case-band case-band--yellow">
    <div class="case-band__sparkles" aria-hidden="true">
      {% include home/sparkle.liquid class="case-band__sparkle case-band__sparkle--1" %}
      {% include home/sparkle.liquid class="case-band__sparkle case-band__sparkle--2" %}
    </div>
    <div class="case-band__inner">
      <p class="case-band__eyebrow">The Brief</p>
      <div class="case-overview">
        {% if page.overview.problem %}
        <div class="case-overview__item">
          <h3>The Problem</h3>
          <p>{{ page.overview.problem }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if page.overview.goal %}
        <div class="case-overview__item">
          <h3>The Goal</h3>
          <p>{{ page.overview.goal }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if page.overview.audience_primary %}
        <div class="case-overview__item">
          <h3>Primary Audience</h3>
          <p>{{ page.overview.audience_primary }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% if page.overview.audience_secondary %}
        <div class="case-overview__item">
          <h3>Secondary Audience</h3>
          <p>{{ page.overview.audience_secondary }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section id="sections" class="case-section">
    <div class="case-section__inner">
      <p class="case-section__label">Explore the campaign</p>
      <h2 class="case-section__title">The PESO Breakdown</h2>
      <p class="case-section__lead">Four channels, each with its own deliverables. Start anywhere &mdash; or read straight through from Paid.</p>

      <div class="pillar-grid">
        {% for pillar in page.pillars %}
        <a class="pillar-card" href="{{ pillar.url | relative_url }}">
          <span class="pillar-card__eyebrow">{{ pillar.label }}</span>
          <h3 class="pillar-card__title">{{ pillar.title }}</h3>
          <p class="pillar-card__desc">{{ pillar.teaser }}</p>
          {% if pillar.items %}
          <ul class="pillar-card__items">
            {% for item in pillar.items %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
          {% endif %}
          <span class="pillar-card__cta">{{ pillar.cta | default: 'View this section' }} &rarr;</span>
        </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% comment %}
  The original deck. Deliberately after the PESO cards: the pillar pages are
  the structured, web-native version and should lead — this is the "see it as
  presented" artifact for anyone who wants the whole thing in one go.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if page.presentation %}
  <section id="deck" class="case-section case-section--tint">
    <div class="case-section__inner">
      <p class="case-section__label">Presentation</p>
      <h2 class="case-section__title">{{ page.presentation.title | default: 'The Full Presentation' }}</h2>
      {% if page.presentation.note %}<p class="case-section__lead">{{ page.presentation.note }}</p>{% endif %}
      <div class="deck-actions">
        {% if page.presentation.canva_url %}
        <a class="deck-actions__primary" href="{{ page.presentation.canva_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v11H4z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M9 20h6M12 16v4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          <span>View the slides</span>
        </a>
        {% endif %}
        {% if page.presentation.pdf %}
        {% include campaign/pdf_link.liquid href=page.presentation.pdf label=page.presentation.pdf_label %}
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if page.citations_pdf %}
  <section class="case-section case-section--tint">
    <div class="case-section__inner">
      <p class="case-section__label">Appendix</p>
      <h2 class="case-section__title">Sources &amp; Citations</h2>
      <p class="case-section__lead">Every statistic and source referenced across the campaign, in full.</p>
      {% include campaign/pdf_link.liquid href=page.citations_pdf label="Download citations (PDF)" %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <footer class="case-footer">
    <a class="button case-footer__cta" href="{{ '/portfolio/' | relative_url }}">&larr; Back to Portfolio</a>
  </footer>

</article>
